From 9815c760fab9e0645d4fada1e8c1f1f2ab40ad99 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: VCKing101 <59761021+VCKing101@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 21:31:39 +1030
Subject: [PATCH] Ad hoc: the wireless switch reads on only once there is a
 session

sceWlanGetSwitchState read on whenever ad hoc play was turned on in the
settings, even with no server hosted or joined. A game then tried to
join, and PortableKit failed the join with an error no PSP gives (its
switch on, a PSP always reaches a group). Dissidia 012 showed that error
(0x80410B05), then left its network half set up: after the player
hosted, Create Room waited for ever with no way out of it.

Now the switch reads on only when ad hoc play is on and there is a
server, hosted or joined (adhoc_server_address()). Before that the game
sees the switch off and says so itself (0x80410B03), and starts cleanly
once the player hosts or joins.

Tested with Dissidia 012 on Windows (two copies) and on the Steam Deck
(native Linux): Create Room with ad hoc on and no session gave the
switch-off error; after Host a session, Create Room made the room and
the other copies found and entered it, then a watched party battle ran
to its end. MSVC framework build, portablekit_host_check and its tests
pass (ad hoc tests left out). Not tested: other games, a game that reads
the switch only once at start.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 host/hle/hle_adhoc.cpp | 10 ++++++++--
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/host/hle/hle_adhoc.cpp b/host/hle/hle_adhoc.cpp
index 9759a8f..c1f3f7a 100644
--- a/host/hle/hle_adhoc.cpp
+++ b/host/hle/hle_adhoc.cpp
@@ -391,9 +391,15 @@ void register_net(HleRegistrar &hle) {
         if (arg(ctx, 0) != 0u) write_mac(rt.memory(), arg(ctx, 0), own_mac());
         done(ctx, "sceWlanGetEtherAddr", 1, 0u, adhoc::format_mac(own_mac()));
     });
-    // The wireless switch is the ad hoc setting: off, the game says so itself.
+    // The wireless switch is on while ad hoc play has somewhere to go: the
+    // setting on, and a server set, hosted or joined. Off, the game says so
+    // itself and starts cleanly once the player hosts or joins. (A switch on
+    // with no server let a game try to join, fail with an error PortableKit
+    // makes up, as no PSP would, and leave its network half set up: Dissidia
+    // 012's next Create Room then waited for ever.)
     hle.add("sceWlanDrv", "sceWlanGetSwitchState", [](Runtime &, AllegrexContext &ctx) {
-        done(ctx, "sceWlanGetSwitchState", 0, settings::current().adhoc ? 1u : 0u);
+        const bool on = settings::current().adhoc && !adhoc_server_address().empty();
+        done(ctx, "sceWlanGetSwitchState", 0, on ? 1u : 0u);
     });
 }
 
